  "instructions": [
    "Heat the olive oil in a large pot over medium heat. Add the onion and cook 4 minutes, until soft and translucent.",
    "Stir in the garlic and ginger. Cook 1 minute, until fragrant.",
    "Add the cumin, coriander, turmeric, and garam masala. Stir for 30 seconds to toast the spices.",
    "Pour in the diced tomatoes with their juice. Cook 3 minutes, stirring often, until the tomatoes break down and thicken slightly.",
    "Add the chickpeas, coconut milk, water, salt, and pepper. Bring to a gentle boil, then lower the heat to medium-low.",
    "Simmer uncovered for 10 minutes, stirring now and then, until the sauce is thick enough to coat a spoon.",
    "Stir in the spinach a handful at a time. Cook 2 minutes, until the leaves are fully wilted.",
    "Taste and add more salt if needed. Serve hot. Cool leftovers fully before storing in the fridge for 4 days or the freezer for 3 months."
  ],
